## Nachtrag 2026-08-06 — verbindlich

Ticket 4 Punkt 3 ist auf \"Header auswerten\" entschieden. Dieses Ticket ist
damit kein Optionsfall mehr, sondern Pflicht: ohne es wäre JS die einzige von
sechs Runtimes mit falschen Pluralformen für nicht-germanische Sprachen.
Priorität auf high gesetzt.
Implemented per mo-reader.md §3 spec, verified against t/data/plural-forms.json.

Files changed:
- js/src/index.js — recursive-descent parser + evaluator for the C-subset
  plural= grammar (ternary/||/&&/comparisons/+-*/%/unary !/parens/n/int
  literals), bounded at depth 100 (§3.3). No eval/new Function. Division and
  modulo by zero evaluate to 0. Missing/unparsable header falls back to
  n != 1 with a one-time console.warn (module-level flag, not per lookup).
  loadTranslations() gained a 4th optional `pluralForms` param (raw header
  string or a pre-parsed {nplurals, evaluate} rule); omitted/null/undefined
  keeps the old n != 1 default *silently* — required for backward compat
  since the 3-arg signature is already published on npm. loadLocaleData()
  now reads header['Plural-Forms'] (po2json passes it through verbatim
  already) and uses it the same way, warning if that key is absent.
- bin/po2json — checked, NO CHANGE NEEDED. It already copies every header
  key (incl. Plural-Forms) into the "" entry unmodified; verified by running
  it against t/data/locale/de_DE/LC_MESSAGES/test.po. The ticket's point 2
  was already satisfied before this ticket started.
- js/src/index.d.ts — loadTranslations() signature + new PluralRule
  interface.
- js/README.md — new "Plural forms" subsection (placed before the existing
  "Deferred translation" section, not touching it) + updated Configuration
  table row.
- js/test/plural-forms.test.js (new) — data-driven over the full
  t/data/plural-forms.json (en/de/fr/pl/ru/ar/ja + the div-by-zero and both
  fallback edge cases), a loadTranslations-2-arg backward-compat test, and a
  dedicated "warns exactly once" test that feeds 3 different broken/missing
  headers through both loadLocaleData and loadTranslations with multiple
  ln() calls each, asserting exactly 1 console.warn total. Kept in its own
  file (Node isolates test files into separate processes) so the
  once-per-process warning flag can't be tripped early by unrelated tests.

Verification:
- `cd js && npm test`: 57/57 pass (46 pre-existing + 11 new).
- `cd js && npm run build`: rollup bundles build clean.
- `dzil test`: currently blocked before reaching the JS run_test step by
  t/50-scrape.t failing on the Perl side — confirmed unrelated to this
